WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:03.854
Line 3 in hall B gets a new filling unit.

2
00:00:04.619 --> 00:00:07.928
It fills the cartons on the belt with product from the tank.

3
00:00:08.987 --> 00:00:12.168
The unit has a frame, a plate, a tank and a cover.

4
00:00:13.321 --> 00:00:14.447
You are the engineer.

5
00:00:15.142 --> 00:00:17.592
You follow the unit from material to line.

6
00:00:18.629 --> 00:00:20.196
That makes six stations.

7
00:00:20.898 --> 00:00:23.731
From strength and machining to welding and moulding.

8
00:00:25.085 --> 00:00:27.941
The first station is Materials and strength.

9
00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.787
The frame has to carry the whole unit.

10
00:00:31.842 --> 00:00:34.536
You choose a steel that can take more than the load.

11
00:00:35.599 --> 00:00:39.175
You check the steel with a tensile test and a hardness test.

12
00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:42.864
Without this the frame can break after months.

13
00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.074
The second station is Machining.

14
00:00:46.778 --> 00:00:49.007
The plate is cut from a block of steel.

15
00:00:50.051 --> 00:00:54.068
A machine cuts metal away until the shape and the holes are right.

16
00:00:55.123 --> 00:00:57.561
You use an end mill and a twist drill.

17
00:00:58.577 --> 00:01:01.282
Without this the holes are not where they should be.

18
00:01:02.557 --> 00:01:05.843
The third station is Process engineering basics.

19
00:01:06.537 --> 00:01:09.196
What is in the tank comes from a process plant.

20
00:01:10.314 --> 00:01:14.423
There the product goes from unit to unit, in batches or continuously.

21
00:01:15.406 --> 00:01:18.668
You use a process flow diagram and a mass balance.

22
00:01:19.674 --> 00:01:23.470
Without this nobody knows what flows, or where product is lost.

23
00:01:24.875 --> 00:01:27.627
The fourth station is Drawings and control.

24
00:01:28.303 --> 00:01:31.426
Frame, plate and tank come together on one drawing.

25
00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:37.066
Whoever reads it sees the shape, the sizes and how exact it must be.

26
00:01:38.048 --> 00:01:41.159
You read the title block and the feature control frame.

27
00:01:42.152 --> 00:01:45.890
Without this maker and customer each measure in their own way.

28
00:01:47.179 --> 00:01:49.698
The fifth station is Welding and joining.

29
00:01:50.393 --> 00:01:53.052
The frame is made of parts that must be joined.

30
00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.984
The seam melts and sets again.

31
00:01:56.748 --> 00:01:58.350
Then the parts are one piece.

32
00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:03.639
You weld with MIG or MAG, and use a welding fixture.

33
00:02:04.668 --> 00:02:06.375
Without this the frame warps.

34
00:02:07.681 --> 00:02:10.235
The sixth station is Injection moulding.

35
00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.275
The cover of the unit is made of plastic.

36
00:02:14.329 --> 00:02:18.102
Molten plastic goes into a mould and cools into a cover.

37
00:02:19.171 --> 00:02:21.423
You use a hot runner and a setting sheet.

38
00:02:22.468 --> 00:02:25.394
Without this the cover gets flash or sink marks.

39
00:02:26.686 --> 00:02:27.917
This is the whole map.

40
00:02:28.633 --> 00:02:32.000
The six stations of Making things lie in one zone.

41
00:02:33.031 --> 00:02:35.051
First Materials and strength.

42
00:02:35.742 --> 00:02:40.166
It covers forces, material strength, fatigue and heat treatment.

43
00:02:41.315 --> 00:02:42.139
Then Machining.

44
00:02:42.871 --> 00:02:45.019
It covers turning, milling and drilling.

45
00:02:45.742 --> 00:02:48.470
Also CNC, tooling and workholding.

46
00:02:49.561 --> 00:02:51.813
Then Process engineering basics.

47
00:02:52.519 --> 00:02:56.746
It covers process types, control, balances and batch capacity.

48
00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:59.560
Then Drawings and control.

49
00:03:00.239 --> 00:03:05.138
It covers reading drawings, tolerances, diagrams and control loops.

50
00:03:06.215 --> 00:03:07.771
Then Welding and joining.

51
00:03:08.459 --> 00:03:12.162
It covers arc welding, spot welding and weld defects.

52
00:03:12.873 --> 00:03:16.205
Also bolts, adhesives and welding in production.

53
00:03:17.302 --> 00:03:19.020
Finally Injection moulding.

54
00:03:19.709 --> 00:03:22.694
It covers the machine, the cycle and plastics.

55
00:03:23.393 --> 00:03:25.645
Also defects, setting and moulds.

56
00:03:26.651 --> 00:03:28.021
That is how they connect.

57
00:03:28.773 --> 00:03:32.802
At strength you pick the material, and the drawing fixes the sizes.

58
00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:36.553
Machining, welding and moulding make the parts.

59
00:03:37.233 --> 00:03:39.346
The process plant makes what goes in.

60
00:03:40.354 --> 00:03:43.628
Each station is a module with four levels per topic.

61
00:03:44.373 --> 00:03:46.242
Start with the part you have to make.
